From 95fed77843d3d93c3e8d3dd0a1aa57493ec45443 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:57:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): priority capture replays
 open<->terminal churn to the final head

The paged priority snapshot is not taken at one head: a row paged late can
already show a later state than an intermediate feed change. check_interval
compared every intermediate change with that row, so a card created or
reopened and then finished inside the ~160 s MacBook capture window (seq
1725387, t_01a1d3a1083e4f69: snapshot done, replayed upsert ready), or any
open<->done flip, refused with "canonical inventory changed". On a busy
board 8 of 8 origins/migrate captures failed (preflight t_01a1d1661daa4ab9).

Replay the feed from the first head through the fixed final head and
compare the FINAL replayed status with each snapshot row:
- status is replayed onto the rows, so a card finishing or reopening in
  the window yields the inventory at the final head (excluded from, or
  added to, the open rows the manifest ranks);
- a card missing from the snapshot that is terminal at the final head
  (created and finished in the window) is out of manifest scope;
- still refused: any in-window id/created_on/priority value differing from
  the row (a real priority change, including one before a completion),
  deletes, malformed/missing uids or statuses, and a card missing from the
  snapshot that is open or of unknown status at the final head.

Snapshot page size is unchanged (client already asks for 1000 rows; the
server cap is outside this change).

Proof: new tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_priority_window_churn.py (created
then completed mid-window, absent or paged late as done; existing card
completed paged before/after; reopened; statusless patches; real priority
/origin/identity changes at every window seq still refuse; membership
refusals). 8 of its tests fail on the old feed module. Mutation run: 10/10
mutants of the new conditions killed. All 18 test files importing
kanban_priority* pass (303 tests). first_head/feed tests that pinned
refusal of a terminal flip now pin its replay from the first head instead.

